WEBVTT

00:00:02.581 --> 00:00:07.516
Riders see problems and ideas first. Now Feedback sits in the custom ride's header,

00:00:07.516 --> 00:00:09.957
and the ride pauses while you write.

00:00:10.324 --> 00:00:15.911
Pick Bug, Improvement or Kudos. The question, its example and the button change with

00:00:15.911 --> 00:00:18.539
it, and a bug attaches diagnostics.

00:00:23.228 --> 00:00:27.926
Every note carries the ride as it stood: the workout, the segment, resistance,

00:00:27.926 --> 00:00:32.442
power, the bike and the last command, listed so you can see what goes.

00:00:36.133 --> 00:00:41.165
Sending locks the form and says so. Once accepted, the thanks fits the kind, and

00:00:41.165 --> 00:00:45.239
Done leaves the ride paused. If it fails, your note is kept.

00:00:49.038 --> 00:00:54.098
Seven acceptance tests failed first and pass now. A bug report carries the last

00:00:54.098 --> 00:00:58.370
megabyte of the packet log and the app version, never a token.

00:01:01.942 --> 00:01:05.916
A bottom sheet on a phone, a popover under the button from tablet up.

00:01:12.266 --> 00:01:16.869
Telo Ride, from the Telo family, turns a smart bike at home into a game.

00:01:17.214 --> 00:01:21.726
It pairs with the bike over Bluetooth, reads your power and sets resistance for

00:01:21.726 --> 00:01:23.397
every hill and interval.

00:01:23.742 --> 00:01:28.920
Two doors: Race (ride a map against your best-time ghost, bots or people) and

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:34.368
Classes (ride along to a video, alone or with a group), fed by one progression of

00:01:34.368 --> 00:01:37.358
XP, rider levels, stars and map unlocks.

00:01:37.704 --> 00:01:40.196
A custom workout lives under Profile.
